{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:24:19Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 122, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Agent", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013vvA1M4oH8aNeu43t46pJE", "input": {"description": "Design keyboard usability for task tracker", "subagent_type": "ux-designer", "run_in_background": false, "prompt": "Read `docs/spec.md` in this repo (`/home/dev/projects/test-project`) \u2014 it's freshly written for Taiga #14 \"Make the app usable from the keyboard\", branch `feature/tp-14/make-app-usable-from-keyboard`. Turn it into `docs/design.md` using your ui-ux-pro-max skill, following the project's own design.md style (there's a previous cycle's design.md in git history at commit 3c8a6a5 / the current docs/design.md before you overwrite it, for \"Give tasks a due date\" \u2014 match its structure/tone).\n\nContext so you don't have to re-derive it: this is a small React (function components, hooks only) + plain-CSS app (`frontend/src/App.css`, no framework, no CSS-in-JS) \u2014 see `CLAUDE.md` for conventions. Every interactive control is already a native element (button/input/select/form), so this design task is narrow: it's about (1) exactly what the `:focus-visible` outline should look like (colour, width, offset) so it reads clearly against every existing background \u2014 including `.filter-option.active` at `frontend/src/App.css:75` (near-black background, `#16191c`) and `.priority-select.priority-high` at `frontend/src/App.css:107-111` (dark orange `#a8480a` background) and `.priority-select.priority-low` at `frontend/src/App.css:113-116` (light grey `#e8eaec` background) \u2014 a single outline colour needs to have sufficient contrast against all of white, near-black, dark orange, and light grey; and (2) confirming/no-op-ing the focus-restoration behavviour the spec already specced out in Acceptance Criteria 4-7 (deleting/completing a row moves focus to a sensible neighbour instead of `<body>`; closing the edit form returns focus to that row's Edit button) \u2014 those are behavioural, not visual, so just note them as \"developer implements per spec, no visual design needed\" rather than re-designing them.\n\nNon-goals already set by the spec: no new ARIA, no global keyboard shortcuts, no skip-link, no other visual changes beyond the focus indicator. Don't design outside that scope.\n\nWrite `docs/design.md` when done, following the shared-conventions rule of naming exact file paths/line numbers so the developer stage doesn't have to re-search."}, "session_id": "dc5f8c4c-3ccf-4cb5-b01c-d37b1d5c560b"}}
