{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:28:17Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 186, "kind": "message", "text": "The design looks solid overall, though I want to flag one thing to the developer: `outline-offset` and box-shadow spread paint over the *surrounding page/container background*, not the button's own fill \u2014 the design doc's contrast math treats the ring as if it sits on top of the button color, which isn't quite how CSS renders it. I'll have the developer implement per design, then verify visually myself with a browser afterward since the developer/reviewer subagents don't have browser tools in this setup. Dispatching **developer** now.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "dc5f8c4c-3ccf-4cb5-b01c-d37b1d5c560b"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:28:35Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 187, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Agent", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DUfoQbF3iNg694k77yKDe2", "input": {"description": "Implement keyboard usability feature", "subagent_type": "developer", "run_in_background": false, "prompt": "Implement Taiga #14 \"Make the app usable from the keyboard\" in `/home/dev/projects/test-project`, on the current branch `feature/tp-14/make-app-usable-from-keyboard`. Read `docs/spec.md` (7 acceptance criteria, non-goals, edge cases, open questions with decided defaults) and `docs/design.md` (the exact `:focus-visible` CSS and behavioural wiring notes) fully before starting \u2014 both are freshly written for this cycle. Then write `docs/implementation.md` documenting what you actually changed, following this project's existing `docs/` style.\n\nQuick orientation (already established, no need to re-derive): this is a small React 19 (function components/hooks only) + plain-CSS frontend at `frontend/src/`, no test infra exists yet (`frontend/package.json` has no `test` script, no test files anywhere) \u2014 that's a pre-existing gap noted in the spec, not something to fix as part of this feature. Every control is already a native `<button>/<input>/<select>/<form>` element, so most of this work is: (1) one CSS `:focus-visible` rule, and (2) focus-management JS in three files.\n\nOne thing to double check as you implement the CSS from `docs/design.md`: the design proposes `outline: 2px solid #0066cc; outline-offset: 2px; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff;` reasoning that the white box-shadow ring will show high contrast against dark button backgrounds like `.filter-option.active` (`#16191c`) and `.priority-select.priority-high` (`#a8480a`). Be aware that an outset `box-shadow` with 0 offset/blur and a positive spread paints in the ring immediately *outside* the element's border box, over whatever is behind the element (the page/container background, e.g. `.task { background: #fff }` at `frontend/src/App.css:28` or `body { background: #f6f7f8 }`), not over the element's own fill colour \u2014 so the \"white ring vs near-black button\" contrast math in the design doc may not hold exactly as computed. Implement the rule as specified, but this is worth a sanity check once it's running \u2014 I'll be verifying focus visibility visually in a browser after your changes land, so if it turns out genuinely hard to see on `.filter-option.active` or `.priority-select.priority-high` once rendered, a reasonable adjustment (e.g. increasing outline width, or making the outline itself the higher-contrast colour choice per element rather than one global rule) is within your judgement \u2014 just document any deviation from the design doc's exact values in `docs/implementation.md` and why.\n\nExact spec/design pointers already gathered for you:\n- AC1 (initial focus): `autoFocus` on the title input in `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx:26-31`.\n- AC4/AC5 (focus after Delete/Done removes a row): needs coordination between `App.jsx` (owns the `tasks` array and knows sibling order) and `TaskList.jsx`'s `TaskRow` (owns the Delete/Done buttons at `TaskList.jsx:127,140`). Compute next-row-else-previous-row-else-AddTask-input per spec AC4, using `task.id`-keyed lookups since the list can be sorted/filtered.\n- AC6/AC7 (focus after edit closes): the Edit button is at `TaskList.jsx:134`; `cancel()` is at `TaskList.jsx:54-58`, `submit()` at `TaskList.jsx:60-69`, Escape/Enter handling at `TaskList.jsx:77-83`. Needs a ref on the Edit button that survives the `isEditing` toggle (it's the same `TaskRow` component instance, not remounted, so a `useRef` in `TaskRow` works directly \u2014 no need to lift this one to `App`).\n- CSS rule per design: end of `frontend/src/App.css`, after line 151.\n\nNon-goals from the spec (don't do these): no new ARIA labels/roles, no custom keyboard shortcuts, no skip-link, no visual changes beyond the focus indicator, no changes to disabled-control behaviour, no backend changes, no new test infra setup (that's the reviewer's call next).\n\nSince there's no test runner yet, verify your JS logic by careful reading/tracing rather than running tests (none exist to run). Run `cd frontend && npm run build` to confirm it type/build-checks cleanly, and `cd frontend && npm run lint` (oxlint) if available, before declaring done. Report exactly what you changed, file by file, and note anywhere you deviated from the design doc."}, "session_id": "dc5f8c4c-3ccf-4cb5-b01c-d37b1d5c560b"}}
