instead, so it can't be occluded by a neighbour and its visibility doesn't depend on what's painted behind the element. All other controls (including `.priority-select.priority-low`) keep the design's original global rule unchanged. This was a judgment call made without browser/screenshot tooling in this session \\u2014 worth a visual confirmation pass.\\n\\n**Verification run:** `cd frontend && npm run build` passes cleanly (production build + JSX type-check via esbuild). `npm run lint` (oxlint) could not be executed \\u2014 every invocation attempt was blocked by this session's command-approval sandbox regardless of how it was invoked; this is an environment constraint, not a discovered lint failure. No frontend test runner exists yet (pre-existing gap noted in `docs/spec.md`), so JS logic was verified by tracing each acceptance criterion by hand against the code rather than via automated tests.\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"agentId: a5781b2fd57909c26 (use SendMessage with to: 'a5781b2fd57909c26', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 85702\\ntool_uses: 48\\nduration_ms: 473922</usage>\"}]", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DUfoQbF3iNg694k77yKDe2", "session_id": "dc5f8c4c-3ccf-4cb5-b01c-d37b1d5c560b"}}
